In article <27t4pf$6f6@news.u.washington.edu>, lazuli@u.washington.edu (Fred Sloniker) writes:
> Where do the names of the dieties in NetHack come from, especially the Tourist
> dieties?  (Preferably, I'd like not just a source, but a brief discussion of
> any interesting personality traits, particularly if the source is not classic
> literature or actual mythology (and thus would require me to track down a
> specific book).)
> 
Tourist deities come from Terry Pratchett's "Discworld" books. If you like
humorous fantasy - this is probably the best on the market. Not only
deities, but also Tourist quest is based on Discworld, and there's even one
Discworld monster in nethack (OK, only when you are hallucinating ;-).
Apparently the Dev. Team likes the books too... Definitely worth tracking
the books down! The other deities are mostly from 'real' mythologies
(except Elven of course ;-) - look the source in pray.c to learn more.

